  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe transitive counterpart of {浮|う}かぶ (to float, to come to mind). Sense 2 is very common in narrative and descriptive writing. The expression {笑|え}みを{浮|う}かべる (to wear a smile) is a standard literary collocation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {船|ふね}を{浮|う}かべる: to float a boat\n- {笑|え}みを{浮|う}かべる: to wear a smile\n- {涙|なみだ}を{浮|う}かべる: to have tears (in one's eyes)\n- {表情|ひょうじょう}を{浮|う}かべる: to show an expression",
